---

<section id="about" class="about">
  <div class="container inner">
    <div class="portrait" data-reveal>
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/img/shoyeb.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img
          src="/img/shoyeb.jpg"
          width="1000"
          height="1250"
          alt="Shoyeb Akhtar"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>

    <div class="text">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h2>Hi, I&rsquo;m Shoyeb.</h2>

      <p>
        I build mobile products, which in practice means I spend most of my time on the
        unglamorous half of the job: working out why a build will not sign, why a crash will
        not reproduce, and why an app that felt quick in the office crawls on a
        three-year-old Android.
      </p>

      <p>
        I came into software sideways &mdash; my degree was engineering, not computer
        science &mdash; and I suspect that is part of why I like the messy end of it.
        Production never hands you a clean problem. Two startups in, both times as the
        person responsible for the app existing at all, and the pattern I keep noticing is
        that the hard part is almost never writing the feature.
      </p>

      <p class="personal">
        Outside of work I would rather see a place with my own eyes than through a lens
        &mdash; I travel when I can, and usually come back without the photos to prove it.
      </p>

      <p class="where">
        Based in Bengaluru, working with teams across the US, UK and Australia.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--section-gap);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 20rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 4rem;
    }
  }

  .portrait {
    max-width: 20rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 6px;
    /* a soft accent edge rather than a drop shadow — reads intentional, not stock */
    outline: 1px solid var(--rule);
    outline-offset: -1px;
  }

  .portrait::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: auto -0.75rem -0.75rem auto;
    width: 60%;
    height: 60%;
    border-right: 2px solid var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 0 6px 0;
    opacity: 0.5;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .text { display: grid; gap: 1.15rem; }

  h2 { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }

  .text > p:not(.label) { color: var(--muted); }

  .personal {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-wash);
  }

  .where {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
